y, takes the first remaining line as the header, and turns each later line into an object keyed by the header fields. A line with a different number of fields than the header throws a `RangeError` whose message contains `line N`, where N is the 1-based line number in the original text, counting the empty lines too. Text with no header gives `[]`.\nR3. `groupTotals(rows, keyField, valueField)` adds up `row[valueField]` for each distinct `row[keyField]`. A value must be a string of the form `12`, `-12`, `12.5` or `12.50` (at most two decimals), and a key must be a string; anything else throws a `TypeError`. The sums are exact, in whole cents, and the result is an array of `{ key, cents }`.\nR4. The result of `groupTotals` is sorted by `cents` from highest to lowest, ties by `key` in plain code-unit order (the order of `<`).\nR5. `renderReport(totals)` takes the result of `groupTotals` (a non-array throws a `TypeError`) and returns one string. Each entry is a line `KEY | AMOUNT`, where the key is padded on the right with spaces to the key width, and the amount is the cents written with thousands separators and exactly two decimals (`123456` is `1,234.56`, `-5` is `-0.05`), padded on the left with spaces to the amount width. After the entries comes a line of `-` characters as long as the entry lines, then a line `TOTAL | AMOUNT` laid out the same way, whose amount is the sum of all the cents. The key width is the length of the longest key, or 5 (the length of `TOTAL`) if that is larger. The amount width is the length of the widest amount, including the total's. The lines are joined with `\\n` with no `\\n` at the end. For an empty list the output is the dashes line and the total line only.\n","tool_call_id":"kEQzNSZ3G3qyes65MvrkSdUF1TVrdoLa"},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"name\":\"report-bugs-task\",\"private\":true,\"type\":\"module\"}\n","tool_call_id":"qvSjnQInohNXwbSXNG2kqb4YOouwJ1ga"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"reasoning_content":"Alright, let's read the so